The ink on Jefferson Parish's short-term rental law was barely dry before property owners began seeking changes. Now some of them are organizing to reverse the ban on renting houses or individual rooms for fewer than 30 days, or at least to modify it so they can stay in business.
Jonathan Perrow of New Orleans, who owns a rental house in Bucktown, said the law represents "an erosion of my rights as a property owner." Plus, he said, he and like-minded owners feel that the Jefferson Parish Council "didn't really talk to us" before adopting the law.
"Reverse the ban" organizers plan to hold a public meeting at 7:30 p.m. July 11 to gather petition signatures and discuss their next steps. The meeting is set at The Rose Garden, 5616 Citrus Blvd., Elmwood.
